7294"},"additionalOsm":[],"rightsStatus":"review-required","geometryStatus":"draft","attribution":"Open Landmarks; contains © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0","references":[{"title":"File:Paris theatre du rond point batiment entier.jpg","author":"Ralf.treinen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_theatre_du_rond_point_batiment_entier.jpg","sourceSha1":"6d310ad6006860cf3c4df9b545bb9f7fd30437a9","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Daytime winter view: low foyer pavilion before broad polygonal roof and a narrow lantern/finial. Trees obscure some rear surfaces."}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["All 22 mapped part heights are retained, including the 10 m auditorium eave, 18 m roof, 20 m lantern and 26 m finial. The surrounding low ranges have tagged 5/6.5 m eaves and 8 m pediments.","The inspected winter street view establishes the low rectangular foyer, broad polygonal roof and narrow central lantern. Windows and cornice thickness are schematic inferences; branches obscure some rear detail.","Closed-volume union removes the parts of foyer roofs buried in the auditorium and the central roof beneath the lantern. Tiny mapped pilasters remain; repeated sculpture, signs and handrails are omitted."],"source":{"url":"/objects/ce784b96f215eae0ab4cb3ba478701943e157a7f60a7d4f6ea8874c3454f472a/source.blend.gz","bytes":145933,"sha256":"ce784b96f215eae0ab4cb3ba478701943e157a7f60a7d4f6ea8874c3454f472a